{"name":"Brown Eyes","hex":"#9e6b4a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brown eyes","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of brown eye"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown_eyes"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bright-line brown-eye","blocks":[{"text":"The bright-line brown-eye is a moth of the family Noctuidae. The species was first described by Carl Linnaeus in his 1758 10th edition of Systema Naturae. It is a common species throughout Europe, but is also found in North Africa, temperate North Asia and Central Asia, Asia Minor, Syria, and Turkestan, northern India, China, Korea and Japan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Lacanobia_oleracea01.jpg/330px-Lacanobia_oleracea01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bright-line_brown-eye"},{"title":"Chaetocneme porphyropis","blocks":[{"text":"Chaetocneme porphyropis, the purple brown-eye or purple dusk-flat, is a species of butterfly of the family Hesperiidae endemic to tropical Queensland, between Innisfail and Daintree on the Atherton Tableland. Its wingspan is about 60 mm. The larvae feed on various Lauraceae species, including Cinnamomum camphora, Cryptocarya grandis, Endiandra compressa, Litsea leefeana, and Neolitsea dealbata."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Chaetocneme_porphyropis_in_Queensland.png/330px-Chaetocneme_porphyropis_in_Queensland.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaetocneme_porphyropis"},{"title":"Brown Eyes (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Brown Eyes (Korean: 브라운아이즈) was a South Korean singing duo that debuted in 2001. They are considered one of South Korea's most important R&B groups, given their immense commercial success."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown_Eyes_(band)"},{"title":"Eye color","blocks":[{"text":"Eye color is a polygenic phenotypic trait determined by two factors: the pigmentation of the eye's iris and the frequency-dependence of the scattering of light by the turbid medium in the stroma of the iris."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Farbverlauf_Augenfarben.jpg/330px-Farbverlauf_Augenfarben.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye_color"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Groente-uil_opgerold_%28Lacanobia_oleracea%29_%2824-08-2006%29.jpg/500px-Groente-uil_opgerold_%28Lacanobia_oleracea%29_%2824-08-2006%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Groente-uil_opgerold_%28Lacanobia_oleracea%29_%2824-08-2006%29.jpg/500px-Groente-uil_opgerold_%28Lacanobia_oleracea%29_%2824-08-2006%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Larva","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGroente-uil_opgerold_(Lacanobia_oleracea)_(24-08-2006).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Lacanobia_oleracea_pupa.jpg/500px-Lacanobia_oleracea_pupa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Lacanobia_oleracea_pupa.jpg/1280px-Lacanobia_oleracea_pupa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Lacanobia_oleracea_pupa.jpg/500px-Lacanobia_oleracea_pupa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pupa","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALacanobia_oleracea_pupa.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Close-up_photograph_of_the_eye_of_a_baby_with_reflection_of_the_scene_in_the_pupil_-_cropped.jpg/500px-Close-up_photograph_o